flowchart TB
    accTitle: The checks of this website
    accDescr: scripts/check.sh runs scripts/check-project.sh last, with the five checks of this website: the tests of its scripts, the format and the rules of their JavaScript, the tables of the projects of projects.toml in README.md and README.de.md, the format, the rules and the types of its Python, and the tests of its hooks. When one fails, the PR coach explains it in the words of .github/checks.project.toml. A table that differs, or code that Biome or Ruff can fix, fixes itself: the job of the check runs .github/mkdocs_project.py --write and scripts/check-project.sh --fix, the fix bot commits what they changed onto the branch of the pull request, and the checks run again; on a pull request from a fork, a person runs those commands and pushes. A test that fails, a line that no test runs, a type or a rule that no tool can fix needs a person, who fixes the code or its test and pushes.

    pull(["A pull request"])
    script["scripts/check-project.sh"]
    scripts["Tests of the scripts<br>of the website"]
    javascript["The format and the rules<br>of the JavaScript"]
    table["The projects of projects.toml<br>in the READMEs"]
    python["The format, the rules<br>and the types of the Python"]
    hooks["Tests of the hooks<br>of the website"]
    coach["The PR coach explains it<br>from .github/checks.project.toml"]
    write[".github/mkdocs_project.py --write<br>scripts/check-project.sh --fix"]
    bot["The fix bot commits the fixes<br>onto a branch of this repository"]
    person(["A person fixes the code<br>or its test and pushes"])

    pull --> script
    script --> scripts & javascript & table & python & hooks
    scripts & javascript & table & python & hooks -- "fails" --> coach
    coach -- "a tool can fix it" --> write
    write --> bot
    bot -. "the checks run again" .-> script
    coach -- "a test or a type fails" --> person
    person -.-> pull

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    class script,scripts,javascript,table,python,hooks,coach,write,bot bot
    class person person
